========================================================================================
 THE DOUBLET-GAP SEQUENCE 4sin^2(pi/2p) (the apex obstruction by prime) and its asymptotics:
========================================================================================
   p= 3: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 1.000000   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 1.096623, ratio 0.9119)
   p= 5: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 0.381966   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 0.394784, ratio 0.9675)
   p= 7: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 0.198062   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 0.201420, ratio 0.9833)
   p=11: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 0.081014   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 0.081567, ratio 0.9932)
   p=13: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 0.058116   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 0.058400, ratio 0.9951)
   p=17: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 0.034054   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 0.034151, ratio 0.9972)
   p=19: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 0.027277   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 0.027340, ratio 0.9977)
   p=23: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 0.018628   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 0.018657, ratio 0.9984)
   p=29: 4sin^2(pi/2p) = 0.011724   (~ pi^2/p^2 = 0.011736, ratio 0.9990)
   => the apex obstruction shrinks like pi^2/p^2; SMALLER odd apex prime = LARGER floor.
      p=7 (the LRC(14) apex) gives 0.198 -- the 3rd-largest (after p=3,5).

========================================================================================
 p mod 4 SPLIT (the Paley/difference-set theme, CLAUDE.md nu_2=0 <=> p=3 mod4):
========================================================================================
   p= 3 (=3 mod4): QR=[1] -> nonzero spectrum {1.0}  PALEY DIFFERENCE SET (flat, |QR-hat(k)|^2=(p+1)/4 const)
   p= 5 (=1 mod4): QR=[1, 4] -> nonzero spectrum {0.382,2.618}  QR symmetric (-1 in QR), NOT a diff-set; 2 spectral values
   p= 7 (=3 mod4): QR=[1, 2, 4] -> nonzero spectrum {2.0}  PALEY DIFFERENCE SET (flat, |QR-hat(k)|^2=(p+1)/4 const)
   p=11 (=3 mod4): QR=[1, 3, 4, 5, 9] -> nonzero spectrum {3.0}  PALEY DIFFERENCE SET (flat, |QR-hat(k)|^2=(p+1)/4 const)
   p=13 (=1 mod4): QR=[1, 3, 4, 9, 10, 12] -> nonzero spectrum {1.6972,5.3028}  QR symmetric (-1 in QR), NOT a diff-set; 2 spectral values
   p=17 (=1 mod4): QR=[1, 2, 4, 8, 9, 13, 15, 16] -> nonzero spectrum {2.4384,6.5616}  QR symmetric (-1 in QR), NOT a diff-set; 2 spectral values
   p=19 (=3 mod4): QR=[1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 11, 16, 17] -> nonzero spectrum {5.0}  PALEY DIFFERENCE SET (flat, |QR-hat(k)|^2=(p+1)/4 const)
   => p=3 mod4 (7,11,19): QR is a Paley difference set (FLAT). p=1 mod4 (5,13,17): QR NOT flat.
      the apex 7=3mod4 is in the Paley/difference-set/flat-QR class (the gap-2 cores exist).
